  {
   "label": "Micropolis M02",
   "kind": "patrol vehicle",
   "description": "The frames show 'MICROPOLIS', the M logo and 'DESIGNED AND MADE IN THE UAE'. Micropolis's own 2025 release gives the M02 10–15 km/h for pedestrian areas (the larger M01 does 40–47 km/h). Gulf News calls the M02 the 'buggy-like' model for narrow roads and dense neighbourhoods. The cameras, 4D imaging radar, face recognition and drone are reported for the patrol vehicles in general. The official unveiling was at the World Police Summit at Expo 2020 (Dubai Exhibition Centre) on 14 March 2022; the user's clip is from January 2022, before that. Not used, because sources conflict: a WhichCar '25 km/h, 450 kg, 10 h' figure for an 'M2', and a Digital Trends '7 km/h, 15 h' figure for an unnamed model. A 'DPR 02' Dubai Police robot launched at GITEX 2025 and Global Village may be the production M02, but that is unconfirmed.",
