 "script": {
  "intro": "This is every robot I've met, from 2013 to 2025. I found most of them at Expo 2020 and GITEX in Dubai, and the first two I built myself.",
  "outro": "Nine robots in twelve years, and I'm still meeting new ones. Thanks for watching, and tell me which one you'd most like to meet.",
  "lines": [
   "That same month, Expo 2020 was a city of its own, with robots around every corner.",
   "There I met two driverless police patrols. This little one is the M02, a self-driving police buggy for narrow streets and neighbourhoods, with its cameras up on a mast.",
   "And this is its big brother, the M01, built for the main roads. Micropolis designed and made it in the UAE with Dubai Police, and it can even launch its own drone.",
   "October 2022, back at GITEX with over a hundred and seventy thousand visitors, and first up, a robot misting disinfectant as it glided through the crowd.",
   "Pepper was everywhere, greeting people. SoftBank built it to read emotions in faces and voices, and made about twenty-seven thousand before pausing production in 2020.",
   "And then Ameca, with the most expressive robot face I've ever seen. Britain's Engineered Arts unveiled it at the end of 2021.",
   "In October 2023, in Busan, my food came on a Dilly S, a serving robot from the Korean delivery app Baemin. Three trays, and about fifteen hours on a charge.",
   "Then NYU Abu Dhabi's stand, with a Spot of their own, kitted out with lidars and cameras for mapping.",
   "The next day I met Ameca again, at the Museum of the Future, where it has greeted visitors since 2022. Its head and face alone have twenty-seven motorised movements, and it chats in more than six languages.",
   "In August 2025, a Promobot V.4 was greeting visitors in a Dubai lobby. It raises itself to your eye level, and its battery lasts up to eight hours."
  ],
